There's a game called "Myth" that is client/server multiplayer nethack-like
game.  I put up a source in ucbvax.berkeley.edu /pub/games a few years ago.
Hope it's still there (haven't checked).

It was written in older C++ (2.0?) and was compiled/tested under g++
version 1.37.  Recently I compiled it on my linux (0.99p8) with
gcc/g++ 2.4.3 but was not able to run it.  You might have better luck
though.

Here is the NAME and DESCRIPTION section from the man page:

------------------------------------------------------------------------------

NAME
       myth - a multiuser screen oriented adventure game.

DESCRIPTION
    	     You  goal  in  life and in myth is to explore a large dun-
       geon, and return  with  The  Amulet  of  Yendor  which  is
       located  somewhere  near the bottom, protected by a mighty
       wizard.

       Myth is a game very similar to rogue,  hack,  moria,  larn
       and omega, but it differs from these games in one signifi-
       cant area: The dungeon is shared by everybody who is play-
       ing  the  game,  and it is possible to meet, fight or help
       the other players.

       If you have not played any of the  above  mentioned  games
       before,  I  will  suggest  that you try out larn or rogue,
       before you start with myth.  You can use most of the  same
       commands in myth as you use in rogue and hack. Press <TAB>
       or <CTRL I> at any time in the game, to get  a  list  over
       which commands to use.

       The  following  options  can be set from the command line.
       -n name is the default name of your character in the game.
       -h  host  is the name of the machine on which myth is run-
       ning.  -b border control how often your view of  the  dun-
       geon  should scroll.  -s force the cover to stay until you
       remove it with <SPACE> -S force the cover  to  be  removed
       when myth don't think you need it anymore.

